{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01PuqBa2LLbPsoWG7QCiakS9", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "62c3d2a4-f30e-4414-bdec-71162c51e62c", "uuid": "cdd6f211-bdeb-4b46-abc7-2786cd62f352", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T13:19:51.492Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01PuqBa2LLbPsoWG7QCiakS9", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "subcommandResults"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcGxBaVxpf9TBKkrE3xt", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I didn't void anything. Here's the message for Dana:\n\n---\n\n**Dana, I haven't voided the Kestrel invoice yet, because that would be a production data change during the freeze. I need your go-ahead first.**\n\n**What I found (read-only):**\n- Kestrel Dental (customer 131) has two open October invoices. Both are for $199.00 and were issued 1 minute apart on 2026-10-01: #402 at 09:00 and #403 at 09:01.\n- Their earlier invoices (#400 and #401) are paid. Nothing else looks duplicated for them.\n- #403 looks like the duplicate. I haven't checked whether anything else points at either invoice, such as payments or reminders.\n\n**What I need from you:** a yes to void #403, which is a single-row status update. It's a small change, but it's still a data change, so it's your call. You can approve it now. You can also wait until after the demo, or have us handle it another way.\n\n**Tonight's billing run:** it's the real risk, because it could send Kestrel another reminder. If you'd rather not touch data, the safer option is to pause or skip Kestrel in that run. That's a change to the job rather than to the database, and it's also your decision.\n\n**Suggested reply to Kestrel:** tell them we know about the duplicate, they owe only one $199.00 invoice, and it's being fixed.\n\nReply \"approve void #403\" and I'll do it and confirm."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 340, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8922, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 340}, "output_tokens": 462, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": n